{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2020-12-30","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2029-06-30","@type":"3"}],"/activity-status@code":"2","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/department/narrative":[{"1":"WCA","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/email":[{"1":"c.savarese@ifad.org"}],"/job-title/narrative":[{"1":"Country Director","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Savarese, Claudia","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"The overall goal of PRIMA is to stimulate regional agricultural trade with a view to creating jobs for women and youth, increasing incomes and improving food security and nutrition for the rural poor. The development objective is to support the sustainable transformation of family farming in Benin and Togo by improving the performance of sub-regional trade centers and cross-border transport corridors, while promoting rural entrepreneurship for young people and women, and fully integrating smallholders into national and sub-regional markets.The development objective is to support the sustainable transformation of family farming through the semi-wholesale markets for agricultural products, promoting rural entrepreneurship of youth and women, and the integration of markets into national, territorial and subregional trade corridors.Rural Infrastructure","@xml:lang":"EN"}]}],"/document-link":[{"/category":[{"@code":"A02"},{"@code":"A07"},{"@code":"A08"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"Benin 2000003066: Regional Programme PRIMA Supervision Report February 2026","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"@format":"APPLICATION/PDF","@url":"https://operations.ifad.org/documents/654016/4c0e0c8d-1fa2-4879-9244-ba0aa5e4066e"},